      "timestamp": "2026-10-13T11:31:44.887+00:00",
      "timestampEdited": null,
      "callEndedTimestamp": null,
      "isPinned": false,
      "content": "Hi! You tell LibreLane what clock period should be achieved using the `CLOCK_PERIOD` variable.\nIf that clock period cannot be achieved for your design, the flow will error out.\n\nOnce you have your chip, you can supply an external clock signal up to that frequency. Of course, you can always supply a lower clock frequency (if you don't use dynamic flip-flops, which is the case for the default SCL).",
